# 🚩 Challenge: [Bit-O-Asm-2]
![alt text](bit-o-asm-2.png)
## 📝 Challenge Description
Can you figure out what is in the eax register? Put your answer in the academy flag format: academy{n} where n is the contents of the eax register in the decimal number base. If the answer was 0x11 your flag would be academy{17}. Download the assembly dump here
.

Hints
1. PTR's or 'pointers', reference a location in memory where values can be stored.
---

### Code / Terminal Snippets
```bash
1. wget https://challenge-files.cylabacademy.net/library/0325d59cb3b29a78bb7872b19f37856d51973b33085362dd4fe5f4cbe7aef80c/disassembler-dump0_b.txt
2. cat disassembler-dump0_b.txt
3. printf "%d\n" 0x9fe1a

or

4. echo "ibase=16; 9FE1A" | bc

or

5. python3 -c "print(0x9fe1a)"

or 

6. python
print(0x9fe1a)

```

---

## 🚀 Exploitation / Solution Path
Detail your step-by-step breakdown to get the flag:
1. Download the `disassembler-dump0_b.txt` file using `wget`.
2. See the content using `cat` command.
3. Open the `python interpreter or cyberchef(ToBase)` to convert the `hexadecimal value to decimal value`
4. The flag will be displayed.

